// One step of the hash, in a word.
//
// `hv * 31` reaches 3.1e10 while the accumulator is still under the modulus, and
// an int is 32 bits -- so the product overflows and the hash comes back negative.
// It is a test, and a test that quietly computes something other than what it
// says is worse than no test at all.

t_pmix(int hv, int v) {
  word wp = hv;
  wp = (wp * 31 + v) % 1000000007;
  int ret_i = wp;
} return int ret_i;
(0, 0):(0)
(1, 2):(33)

// Test-only fixture: a small real truecolour+alpha PNG (borrowed from the spr
// project, which already exercises it), so t_hash/t_row's own 4-byte-a-pixel
// stride has a genuine RGBA image to walk without decoding the 2560x2560
// sheet main.id uses (see png_ready in main/tail.id).
png_rgba_ready() {
  png_ready();
  inf_init();
  png_load("../spr/img/rgba.png");
} return void;
():() then calls png_ready:[1]
